# Normalise to LF in the repository, whatever the checkout platform does.
#
# Two things here bite otherwise. A CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for
# an interpreter called "/bin/sh\r", which fails with a message that never
# mentions newlines. And the dependency pin hash - the key for the prebuilt
# tarballs and the CI cache - is taken over the bytes of cmake/*.cmake, so
# a checkout that disagreed about line endings would compute a different
# hash and silently miss every cache and every prebuilt.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
*.jar binary
